     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>Hi all,<div><br></div><div>I wonder how can I save an output from renderText (for example) into .doc file? Suppose I have raw HTML like this in server.R and htmlOutput() in ui.R </div><div><br></div><div>### server.R</div><div><br></div><div>output$Conclusion &lt;- renderText({<br></div><div>      paste(&quot;&lt;div style = &#39;color: #4187C5; font-size: 1.1em; font-weight: bold;&#39;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Statistical analysis&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&quot;)<br></div><div><br></div><div>})</div><div><br></div><div>I would like to save the output from renderText into .doc file. I have tried to use rtf-package, but it saves raw HTML code as well.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks much!</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "2Fz6c-7nnrMJ",
   "from": "Barb Banbury",
   "author": "4ff0cd0800ebb0b6",
   "date": "2014-09-04T19:32:54Z",
   "subject": "Re: Saving reactive objects into .doc",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">You can easily save them as text files using the download handler function.<div><br></div><div>In server.R add in a new output function:</div><div><br></div><div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p></p><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">  output$textOut </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> downloadHandler</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    filename </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\">paste</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">NAME</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;.txt&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)},</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    content </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">file</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      write</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">what you want to save to file</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> file</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)})</span></div></code></div><p></p><div>And then in the ui.R, you will need to add some kind of button to download. </div><div><span><br></span></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">downloadButton</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;textOut&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> label</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Download text file&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><div><p><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><br></span></p><p><span style=\"line-height:normal\">I don&#39;t know about saving as a .doc that preserves HTML formatting, so sorry if this is no help at all. </span><br></p></div><div><br></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
