i.R, you will need to add some kind of button to download. </div><div><span><br></span></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">downloadButton</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;textOut&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> label</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Download text file&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><div><p><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><br></span></p><p><span style=\"line-height:normal\">I don&#39;t know about saving as a .doc that preserves HTML formatting, so sorry if this is no help at all. </span><br></p></div><div><br></div></div></div></blockquote></div>"
